            <ArticleTitle>Preseptal cellulitis in a child caused by Megacopta centrosignatum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaapos.2012.08.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1091-8531(12)00323-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Preseptal cellulitis in children can be caused by a reaction to embedded insects, their body parts, or secretions. We report the case of a 2-year-old girl who presented with preseptal cellulitis caused by an insect identified as Megacopta centrosignatum in her superior fornix.</AbstractText>
